# Understanding AI

#### Understanding how AI generates text can help prevent falling into the pitfalls in the previous levels. The most important thing to understand about AI is its relationship to reality. AI models do not perceive the world—they generate text solely based on patterns learned from language.

#### Because of this, AI can produce fluent, convincing text, but it depends entirely on humans to supply grounding, verify accuracy, and interpret results. Misunderstandings often occur when users expect AI to “know” facts or reason logically, when in reality it is only producing statistically likely sequences of words.

<div style="text-align: center; width: 80%; margin: 0 auto;">
  <p style="
    font-size: 18px; 
    background-color: #F5F7F8; 
    padding: 10px; 
    border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; 
    border-right: 5px solid #8148B2;
    display: inline-block;
  ">
    AI predicts and generates language patterns extremely well, but humans must provide context, verify outputs, and make final decisions.
  </p>
</div>

